# Local env files — never commit real tokens
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local runtime state written next to the project. Never a source file, never
# commit it.
# Scoped to the repo root only — an unscoped "data/" also matched src/data/**,
# silently dropping the Instagram source of truth (types.ts, instagram-posts.json)
# at commit time. Confirmed via `git check-ignore -v`.
/data/

# Local design-tooling state. Re-installable, not part of the product, and not
# something to commit to a public site.
.claude/
.impeccable/

# The design tool's own working files (root only) -- not product source.
/PRODUCT.md
/DESIGN.md

# Internal working papers: reports, screenshots, evidence. Never published.
/reports/

# Internal working documents (process notes, plans, evidence, diagrams). The
# master copy lives outside this repository and is mirrored in while work is in
# progress; none of it is published.
#
# Scoped to the repo root on purpose: an unscoped "team/" would also hide any
# src/**/team/** that ever appears. The two real docs in docs/ -- DEPLOYMENT.md
# and INSTAGRAM.md -- are tracked product documentation and stay tracked.
/docs/team/
/docs/verify/
/docs/diagrams/
/docs/plans/
/docs/TEAM-RULES.md
/docs/PLACEHOLDERS.md
/STATUS.md
